(version 1)

# Custom DRC rules for RejsaCAN v3.5.
#
# Board-setup constraints hold the JLCPCB floors. These rules cover what a flat
# global constraint cannot express.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Automotive spacing on the raw car supply.
#
# CORRECTED: the earlier version of this rule cited IPC-2221 table 6-1 row B2
# and called 0.35mm a compromise against a "required" 0.6mm. That was the wrong
# column. Table 6-1 is indexed by COATING, not by layer:
#
#   B1  internal conductors                     0.10mm  (31-50V and 51-100V)
#   B2  external, UNCOATED                      0.60mm
#   B4  external, permanent polymer coating     0.13mm  <-- this board
#   A6  external, uncoated, TERMINATIONS/pads   0.40mm @31-50V, 0.50mm @51-100V
#
# Every track on this board is under solder mask, so B4 applies and asks 0.13mm.
# 0.35mm is 2.7x that, not a shortfall. The old "raise to 0.6mm on the 4-layer
# respin" note was chasing B2 and has been removed -- it was tried on 4 layers
# and cost the power corner its routability for no electrical gain.
#
# Design band: the board is offered for 5-24V systems, so ISO 16750-2 applies
# (regulator failure 34V/60min, centrally-suppressed load dump ~58V) -> the
# 51-100V row is the one to design to. B4 is still 0.13mm there.
#
# Scoped to tracks: pad-to-pad spacing is set by the parts, see rule 4.
# Covers Battery (VCC) AND Battery_Out (VBAT_IN, the raw pre-fuse input).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(rule "automotive battery track spacing"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.35mm))
	(condition "(A.NetClass == 'Battery' || A.NetClass == 'Battery_Out') && A.Type == 'Track'"))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Documented exception: USB-C board-lock holes.
#
# The GT-USB-7010ASV puts its NPTH board locks 0.1944mm from the plated GND
# through-holes. That is the vendor's own geometry, and it is below JLCPCB's
# published hole-to-hole spacing -- but the fabricated v3.4 board carries it, so
# JLC evidently accepts it on this part.
#
# Narrowed to pairs inside USBC1 so the exception cannot silently excuse a real
# hole-spacing problem anywhere else on the board.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(rule "USB-C vendor board-lock hole spacing (accepted exception)"
	(constraint hole_clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('USBC1') && B.memberOfFootprint('USBC1')"))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Bare battery-voltage pads.
#
# Pads are uncoated metal, so IPC-2221 row A6 governs them, not B4: 0.50mm at
# 51-100V. Bare copper at battery potential is where condensation and salt
# actually bridge -- mask-covered track spacing is not the exposure.
#
# This rule exists to make that exposure VISIBLE in DRC. Violations here are not
# routing errors; they are component-choice consequences (an 0402 land pattern
# cannot yield 0.5mm). Fix by moving the offending passive to 0603/0805, not by
# rerouting.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excludes pads of the SAME footprint: IPC-2221 governs BOARD conductor spacing,
# whereas the gap between two pins of one package is fixed by that package and is
# covered by the component's own qualification. U4 is a TSOT-23-6 on 0.95mm pitch
# -- no board rule can widen it, and flagging it every build is noise that hides
# the violations that ARE actionable.
(rule "bare battery-voltage pad spacing (IPC-2221 A6)"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.50mm))
	(condition "(A.NetClass == 'Battery' || A.NetClass == 'Battery_Out') && A.Type == 'Pad' && B.Type == 'Pad' && !A.sameFootprintAs(B)"))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Pad-to-pad spacing is set by the parts, not by the router.
#
# With the footprints corrected to the geometry actually fabricated, U2's real
# 2.045mm pads come within 0.189mm of C11 -- that is the board that was built and
# is working. JLCPCB's floor for SMD pads on different nets is 0.15mm, so it is
# manufacturable; it is only under the 0.2mm the net classes ask of *routing*.
#
# NARROWED: this used to be an unscoped "any pad against any pad" rule, which
# silently granted 0.15mm to every pad on the board including battery-voltage
# ones. It is now limited to the specific as-fabricated pairs it was written for.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(rule "as-fabricated component pad spacing (U2/C11)"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('U2') && B.memberOfFootprint('C11')"))

(rule "as-fabricated component pad spacing (C11/U2)"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('C11') && B.memberOfFootprint('U2')"))
